{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Comment sync (append-only) with persistent Jira-comment-ID map + rich rendering\n\n## Context / Problem\nComment sync currently identifies comments by **body equality** (a normalized-text\nkey computed in `outbound_comments._diff_comments`), which is fragile: two comments\nwith the same text collide, and an edited body looks like a brand-new comment. The\nin-code note at `outbound_comments.py` (`\"PR #402 … ID-based binding once available;\nthis body-equality match is the baseline\"`) already anticipates the fix. The team\nhas settled comment semantics as **append-only** — mirror comment *creation* both\nways, but do not sync edits or deletes — which keeps the design simple and matches\nthe reconciler's existing inbound behavior of skipping already-known Jira comment IDs.\n\nThis story ALSO **owns the DC comment-diff dedup-key migration that `3388`\ndeliberately deferred here.** `3388` redefines `WikiTextCodec.normalize_outbound`\nfrom identity to the rendering form for descriptions, but keeps the comment-diff\npath injecting the plain/identity normalizer UNCHANGED (via the a32a `_resolve_codec`\nseam, defaulting to `_IdentityCodec`) so the description cutover does not shift the\ncomment dedup key. Flipping the comment path to the real rendering codec — and\nkeeping comment-diff convergent when it renders rich — is this story's job, not\n`3388`'s.\n\n## Approach\nTwo coupled changes, both append-only and echo-safe:\n\n1. **Stable identity by a local comment key + the returned Jira ID, not body.** Each\n   rebar comment originates from a COMMENT event whose **HLC `timestamp`** (unique,\n   monotonic; already threaded onto the compiled comment entry at\n   `reducer/_processors.py:349`, alongside `author`) is the **stable local comment\n   identity** — nothing else on the entry (`body`/`author`/`source_*`) is\n   collision-proof once body-equality is abandoned. Maintain a **persistent map\n   `local_comment_key (HLC) → Jira comment ID`** in the binding state. Outbound: when\n   rebar has a comment whose local key has no mapped Jira ID, create it in Jira and\n   record the returned Jira comment ID against that local key. Inbound: mirror Jira\n   comments whose IDs are not already values in the map as new rebar comments (whose\n   entries carry the existing `jira_comment_id`, bug 85a1 `_processors.py:354-356`,\n   the inbound half of this identity). **Append-only**: never push rebar edits/deletes\n   to Jira comments and never apply Jira comment edits/deletes to rebar — an\n   already-mapped key/ID is never re-synced (the ID map is the durable echo guard for\n   comments, superseding the body-key match and complementing the existing\n   `RECONCILER_MARKER` machine-comment guard, `outbound_comments.py:72/177-184`,\n   which still excludes bridge-internal payloads). The ID map is change-gated and\n   fixed-shape (one small entry per comment, added once) to respect epic `0303`'s\n   churn discipline.\n1a. **Capture the returned Jira comment ID at the enactment sites (the missing\n   write-back data path).** The Jira comment ID is only obtainable as\n   `SupportsComments.add_comment`'s return value — a `dict[str, Any]` carrying\n   `{\"id\": …}` (`_backend.py:491`; both transports return this shape —\n   `adapters/jira/backend.py:265` for Cloud, `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py:433`\n   for DC), but **both enacting sites currently DISCARD it**:\n   `dispatch_one.py:418` (create path) and `dispatch_apply_phases.py:165` (update\n   path). This story changes both sites to read the returned dict, extract the id, and\n   write `{local_comment_key: jira_id}` into the binding-store comment-ID map,\n   confirming the id-key extraction is uniform across the Cloud (acli) and DC\n   (jira_datacenter) transports. Failures stay non-fatal exactly as today (the\n   existing `comment_errors` capture is unchanged); only a successful create records a\n   mapping.\n2. **Render comment bodies through the codec, and migrate the dedup key.** Outbound\n   comment bodies are rendered through the SAME `RichTextCodec.to_wire` seam the\n   descriptions use (`adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py` — `AdfCodec.to_wire` for\n   Cloud, the now-rendering `WikiTextCodec.to_wire` for DC after `3388`), applied in\n   `_map_comments_for_create`/`_decorate_outbound_comment`. To keep the local\n   comparison key aligned with the rendered wire, this story **flips the a32a codec\n   injection** (`_diff_comments`'s `_resolve_codec` argument, `outbound_comments.py`)\n   from the default `_IdentityCodec` to the real `RichTextCodec`, so the local dedup\n   key is `normalize_outbound`-consistent with what lands on Jira. Because identity\n   is now the ID map, the dedup key is only a secondary guard, so the migration\n   cannot reintroduce duplicate re-posts: an AC asserts DC comment-diff still\n   converges (zero duplicate re-post) after the injection flip. This is the mirror\n   of `3388`'s `test_dc_comment_diff_unchanged_by_cutover` (which pinned the key\n   UNCHANGED under the description-only cutover); here it changes deliberately and\n   still converges.\n\nDescriptions + the description cutover ship first (`e59d`/`271c`/`3388`, on which\nthis story depends), so this builds on the codec-rendering + state-echo-suppression\nalready in place.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py` — persistent per-binding\n  comment-ID map `local_comment_key → jira_id` (change-gated, append-only,\n  fixed-shape entry).\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py` (`:418`, create path) and\n  `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_apply_phases.py` (`:165`, update path)\n  — capture `add_comment`'s returned `dict[str, Any]` (`{\"id\": …}`), extract the id\n  uniformly across the Cloud (acli) and DC transports, and write it into the\n  binding-store comment-ID map against the originating comment's local key; keep the\n  existing non-fatal `comment_errors` behavior.\n- `src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py` — surface the COMMENT event's stable local key\n  (the HLC `timestamp`, already on the entry at `:349`) so the differ can associate a\n  returned Jira id with the originating comment; no new per-pass state.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/outbound_comments.py` — comment differ keyed\n  by the ID map (via the local comment key) instead of the normalized body key;\n  outbound create renders via `RichTextCodec.to_wire` in\n  `_map_comments_for_create`/`_decorate_outbound_comment`; flip the `_diff_comments`\n  a32a codec injection (`_resolve_codec`) from `_IdentityCodec` to the real\n  `RichTextCodec` for the local dedup key; preserve the `RECONCILER_MARKER`\n  machine-comment exclusion.\n- inbound comment mirror path — mirror only Jira comment IDs absent from the map;\n  never apply Jira comment edits/deletes.\n- `tests/` — comment identity, id-capture data-path, append-only, rendering, and\n  dedup-key-migration convergence tests.\n\n## Testing\n- Duplicate bodies: two rebar comments with identical text create two distinct Jira\n  comments and map to two distinct IDs (no collision), keyed by ID not body.\n- Idempotence: a second reconcile pass creates 0 duplicate comments (mapped IDs are\n  skipped).\n- Append-only: a rebar comment edit does not push to Jira and a Jira comment edit\n  does not overwrite rebar; only genuinely new comments mirror.\n- Rich rendering: an outbound comment body is rendered through `RichTextCodec.to_wire`\n  (Cloud ADF / DC wiki), asserted by the wire shape a create receives.\n- Dedup-key migration convergence: after flipping the comment `_resolve_codec`\n  injection to the real rendering codec, DC comment-diff still converges with zero\n  duplicate re-post (the deliberate counterpart to `3388`'s\n  `test_dc_comment_diff_unchanged_by_cutover`).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Comment identity is a persistent map from a stable local comment key (the\n  COMMENT event HLC) to the Jira comment ID, not the normalized-body key; verified by\n  `test_comment_duplicate_bodies_distinct_ids` (two identical-text comments map to\n  two IDs).\n- [ ] The returned `add_comment` `{\"id\": …}` dict is captured at both enactment sites\n  (`dispatch_one.py` create, `dispatch_apply_phases.py` update) and persisted against\n  the originating comment's local key, with the id extraction uniform across the Cloud\n  (acli) and DC transports; verified by `test_comment_id_captured_and_persisted`\n  (fake client returns `{\"id\": \"1\", …}`; the map records it).\n- [ ] Comment sync is append-only in both directions — new comments mirror once,\n  edits/deletes are not synced; verified by `test_comment_append_only` (an\n  edit/delete triggers no cross-side write).\n- [ ] Outbound comment bodies are rendered through the shared `RichTextCodec.to_wire`\n  seam (Cloud ADF / DC wiki), and the `_diff_comments` a32a codec injection is\n  migrated from `_IdentityCodec` to the real rendering codec so the local dedup key\n  matches the landed wire; verified by `test_comment_rendered_through_codec` and\n  `test_comment_dedup_key_uses_real_codec`.\n- [ ] After the dedup-key migration, DC comment-diff converges with zero duplicate\n  re-post (the deliberate counterpart to `3388`'s comment-diff-unchanged pin);\n  verified by `test_dc_comment_diff_converges_after_migration`.\n- [ ] A repeat reconcile pass creates no duplicate comments; verified by\n  `test_comment_sync_idempotent`.\n- [ ] The comment-ID map is change-gated and adds no per-pass churn (fixed-shape,\n  one entry per comment, added once); verified by the git-delta cost harness on a\n  no-new-comment pass."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785822463746262001,"uuid":"434c2e1c-ab13-4c9b-8226-213f528beaa0"}